  "limits": [
    "A perceptual hash only catches near-identical copies (same picture, rescaled, recompressed or lightly noisy; mirrored copies are checked separately). A crop, a different photograph of the same canvas or a colour-only change can slip through.",
    "Unknown Artist is 48% of the images and each one is its own split group, so the artist-disjoint guarantee covers named painters only. This audit cannot tell whether two unknown paintings share a hand.",
    "The shard is where an image sat in the source dataset (5 shards here, chosen to build the classes), not something a model sees. The shard floor measures a construction bias; it is not a feature any model has.",
